Xplanet normally uses its built-in planetary positions. For a render that
needs a higher-precision ephemeris, use -ephemeris_file with a native JPL
binary. The ephemeris itself is not bundled.

The little-endian DE440 file linux_p1550p2650.440 has been checked against
JPL's reference data for Cartesian positions and velocities. Download it
from the JPL native binary directory:

https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/ftp/eph/planets/Linux/de440/

For example:

xplanet -ephemeris_file /path/to/linux_p1550p2650.440 -target earth \
  -date 20260320.120000 -num_times 1 -output earth-de440.png

Use a file covering the render date. SPICE .bsp files use a different
reader; see the spice README. The native reader is based on Bill Gray's
work: https://www.projectpluto.com/jpl_eph.htm
